          "message": {
            "text": "panic-unwrap: unwrapping a `parse::<u64>()` on a URL path segment supplied by the client (`/users/<id>`). Any non-numeric id (e.g. `/users/abc`) panics the handler thread, killing that connection (and, without a panic hook/thread isolation, potentially taking down the service). Use `match`/`?` and return 400 instead."
          },
          "ruleId": "panic-unwrap"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
