                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 26,
                  "startLine": 26
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "panic-unwrap: `TcpListener::bind(...).expect(\"bind to 8080\")` aborts the process if the port is already in use or unavailable. The listen address is also hard-coded; return the `io::Result` from a `try_main`/`run()` and log + exit with a non-zero status instead of panicking."
          },
          "ruleId": "panic-unwrap"
        },
        {
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "crates/svc-core/src/models.rs"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 29,
                  "startLine": 29
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "panic-unwrap: `raw.split(',').next().unwrap()` on caller/user-supplied `raw`. `split` yields at least one item for any input, so today it happens not to panic, but the unwrap encodes an unverified assumption; if the iterator source is ever changed (e.g. to a filtered/peeked iterator) this panics inside a request path. Use `next().unwrap_or_default()` or a `match`, or simply `raw.split(',').next()?` style handling returning `Option`."
          },
          "ruleId": "panic-unwrap"
        }
